{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Now the man Moses was very humble.</b> The verse tells you that he did not take her out of arrogance, but there was a cause and a circumstance, and even so he was humble, for he did not demand justice for his own humiliation — until the Holy One, blessed be He, came and demanded it." "<b>ענו.</b> It is written defective yod, to say that he was humble in all his limbs. For when you write the letters of ענו by their names — ayin, nun, vav — you find that it totals 248 limbs:"], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:16.788591990Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}